The paper’s main dichotomy is now clear: unit-length/unit-cost SLSN is polynomial for a constant number of demands, FPT for star demands, and W[1]-hard for any recursively enumerable demand class that has unbounded size and is not restricted to stars. I’m reading the reduction details next, because those determine whether a planted witness can be carried through construction and whether the generated distribution has an honest hardness claim.
