codex
The result is correctly parked as `cap_bound`—not shipped and not rejected.

The generator uses the paper’s \(H_{2,k}\) reduction from Section 4.2.3. All local gates pass, but the oracle pool solved every instance through \(n=60\); \(n=62\) would require 302 intended operations, exceeding the 300-operation cap. This is consistent with the paper’s distinction between tractable star/constant-demand cases and W[1]-hard general demand structures. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.10566)

Deliverables:

- [gen_1802_10566.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.10566/gen_1802_10566.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.10566/selftest_report.json)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.10566/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.10566/README.md)
- [.meta.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.10566/.meta.json)

Key measurements:

- 0/200,000 random guesses succeeded.
- Five attacks succeeded on 0/8 seeds each.
- Reference path consistency solved 8/8, averaging 141,608 tests.
- Answer: 319 characters, 58 atoms.
- Intended route: 282 operations.
- Oracle: hard 3/3 solved; escalated \(n=60\) 3/3 solved.
- Final verdict: `cap_bound`.

The hinted/placebo G9 arms were not run because the task explicitly requires stopping at `cap_bound`; no transcripts were fabricated.
